  "reason": "Evidence: config_020 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is our best at 0.6352 acc / 0.6183 F1, and weighted fusion clearly beats concat (config_020 vs config_001). RNA dominates (0.5907) while image alone is weak (0.3316), but the multimodal combination adds ~4-5 points over RNA-only. Uncertainty: We have only tested avgpool aggregation; transformer aggregation is completely unexplored and could capture richer cross-profile interactions. Question: Does transformer aggregation improve over avgpool when all other settings (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, multiprofile) are held constant? Why this is best: config_022 is a clean single-variable extension of our best-performing config, isolating the aggregation effect. Under a limited budget, testing the most impactful unexplored design axis (aggregation) on top of the strongest known configuration maximizes information gain per experiment and directly builds on the strongest evidence we have."
}

